---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';import {blockLessons} from '../../lib/blocks/curriculum.mjs';import '../../styles/blocks.css';
const groups=[...new Set(blockLessons.map(l=>l.group))];
---
<Layout title="Programming Basics for Kids — 20 Visual Coding Lessons | Kids Code" description="Learn variables, data types, if/else, loops, lists, dictionaries, functions, and debugging with 20 interactive block coding tasks for kids."><div class="wrap"><section class="block-path-hero"><div class="page-head"><span class="pill">✦ NEW · The programming foundations trail</span><h1 style="margin-top:22px">Big coding ideas.<br/>One little block<br/>at a time.</h1><p>Learn the building blocks of programming by snapping them together. Give Bit instructions, watch your variables change, and turn “what does that mean?” into “I made it work!”</p><div class="actions"><a class="button dark" href="/blocks/sequences/">Start with lesson one →</a><a class="button ghost" href="/blocks/playground/">Just let me build</a></div><div class="hero-proof"><span>20 guided tasks</span><span>No code typing needed</span><span>Save your creations</span></div></div><div class="block-sticker-stack" aria-hidden="true"><div class="visual-block">when I press Run ▶</div><div class="visual-block">set curiosity to <b>100</b></div><div class="visual-block">if <b>idea = awesome</b></div><div class="visual-block">repeat <b>try something!</b> ↻</div></div></section><div class="note"><strong>Like Scratch-style coding?</strong> This is our own visual playground, powered by Blockly. Snap blocks together, run them on Bit’s stage, and test your ideas. You can also turn your blocks into Python when you’re ready. A computer or larger tablet gives the canvas more room; the text fields still need a little typing.</div><section><span class="eyebrow">Programming basics for kids</span><h2>Your map from “hello”<br/>to “I built an algorithm.”</h2><p>Each mission has a short explanation, starter blocks, a goal, a hint, and checks that run your actual program. Start at the beginning or jump to something you’re curious about.</p>{groups.map((group,i)=><section class="block-course-group"><span class="eyebrow">Chapter {i+1}</span><h2>{group}</h2><div class="lesson-list">{blockLessons.filter(l=>l.group===group).map(l=><a class="lesson-item" href={'/blocks/'+l.slug+'/'}><span class="lesson-number">{String(l.index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{l.title}</h3><p>{l.topic} · {l.time} min</p></div><span class="completion" data-completion={'blocks-'+l.slug}>Try it</span></a>)}</div></section>)}</section><section class="section"><div class="cta-band"><div><span class="eyebrow">No goal. No rules to invent for you.</span><h2>What if you made<br/>something completely yours?</h2><p>All the blocks. An open stage. Your imagination.</p></div><a class="button dark" href="/blocks/playground/">Open the free playground ↗</a></div></section><p class="blocks-credit">Block Lab uses <a href="https://blockly.com/">Blockly</a>. It is an independent Kids Code learning experience, not the Scratch editor or an official Scratch product.</p></div></Layout>
